values ('b30c8d37-6cd6-59ea-a263-16ac77ce6096', 'd61286c0-e727-52d1-b7af-a1519069ad03', (select t.id from public.topics t join public.subjects s on s.id = t.subject_id where s.slug = 'mathematics' and t.name = 'Angles of Elevation and Depression'),
        'A kite is flying on a straight string 50 m long. The kite is 35 m above the hand holding the string. Find the angle of elevation of the kite from the hand, correct to the nearest degree.',
        null,
        'The string is the hypotenuse and the height is opposite the angle:

$\sin\theta = \dfrac{35}{50} = 0.7$, so $\theta = \sin^{-1} 0.7 = 44.4° \approx 44°$.

**Why the other options are wrong**

- 35°: You used tan. The string, 50 m, is the hypotenuse, so use sin.
- 46°: You used cos. The height is opposite the angle, so use sin.
- 55°: You worked out $\tan^{-1}\dfrac{50}{35}$. The height is opposite the angle and the string is the hypotenuse.',
