insert into public.questions (id, paper_id, topic_id, stem, image_url, explanation, position)
values ('128b1b5e-85dc-5d8a-9923-cf765739dc8e', 'd61286c0-e727-52d1-b7af-a1519069ad03', (select t.id from public.topics t join public.subjects s on s.id = t.subject_id where s.slug = 'mathematics' and t.name = 'Angles of Elevation and Depression'),
        'A man whose eyes are 1.8 m above the ground stands 20 m from the foot of a tree on level ground. The angle of elevation of the top of the tree from his eyes is 30°. Find the height of the tree, correct to one decimal place.',
        null,
        'Height above his eyes $= 20 \tan 30° = 20 \times 0.57735 = 11.547$ m.

Height of the tree $= 11.547 + 1.8 = 13.347 \approx 13.3$ m.

Don''t round 11.547 before adding: examiners often penalise early rounding.

**Why the other options are wrong**

- 11.5 m: You forgot to add the height of his eyes above the ground, 1.8 m.
- 11.8 m: You used sin. The 20 m is adjacent to the angle, so use tan.
- 13.4 m: You rounded too early: $11.547$ became $11.55$, giving $13.35$ and then $13.4$. Keep the full value until the last step.',
        4)
