values ('328ba125-1339-5c69-89dd-7d1769044bb5', '20685801-a723-5988-869a-2436c20a2491', (select t.id from public.topics t join public.subjects s on s.id = t.subject_id where s.slug = 'mathematics' and t.name = 'Bearings'),
        'A ship sails 8 km due north from port $P$ to $Q$, then 6 km due east to $R$. Find the bearing of $R$ from $P$, correct to the nearest degree.',
        'https://wasscetutor.com/questions/mathematics/maths-bearings-04.svg?v=30d382a62a',
        'At $P$, measure clockwise from north. In the right-angled triangle $PQR$:

$\tan\theta = \dfrac{6}{8} = 0.75$, so $\theta = 36.9°$.

The bearing of $R$ from $P$ is $037°$.

**Why the other options are wrong**

- 053°: You worked out $\tan^{-1}\dfrac{8}{6}$, the angle measured from east. A bearing is measured from north: $\tan\theta = \dfrac{6}{8}$.
- 143°: $180° - 37°$ would point south-east. $R$ is north-east of $P$.
- 323°: $360° - 37°$ would point north-west. $R$ is east of north, so the bearing is less than 090°.',
