values ('2f45e245-b76e-5ed6-a357-0cd3a78e37e6', '7077c368-6fb6-5fed-a6c1-12ab6ca06fbc', (select t.id from public.topics t join public.subjects s on s.id = t.subject_id where s.slug = 'mathematics' and t.name = 'Logarithms'),
        'Express $\log 4 + 2\log 3 - \log 6$ as the logarithm of a single number.',
        null,
        '$2\log 3 = \log 3^{2} = \log 9$.

$\log 4 + \log 9 - \log 6 = \log\dfrac{4 \times 9}{6} = \log 6$

**Why the other options are wrong**

- $\log 4$: $2\log 3 = \log 3^{2} = \log 9$, not $\log 6$.
- $\log 7$: You added and subtracted the numbers: $4 + 9 - 6$. Adding logs means multiplying, subtracting means dividing.
- $\log 216$: You multiplied all three. Subtracting a log means dividing: $\dfrac{4 \times 9}{6}$.',
        4)
